

(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[1 1 "//go:build linux"] [15 1 "// The module _posixsubprocess (PY6e; Modules/_posixsubprocess.c): fork_exec over Go's syscall.ForkExec, the only"] [16 1 "// way a multithreaded Go program starts a child. The child's descriptors are ForkExec's Files: 0, 1 and 2 the"] [17 1 "// pipes' ends (or inherited), pass_fds kept at their numbers, with close_fds every other open descriptor closed. A"] [18 1 "// failed exec is reported as CPython's child reports it, on errpipe_write (\"OSError:<hex errno>:\" and \"noexec:chdir\""] [19 1 "// for a bad cwd), with a pid that is no child (waitpid's ChildProcessError, which subprocess ignores). preexec_fn"] [20 1 "// cannot run (no Python in the child between fork and exec): it raises."] [22 1 "// noChildPid is the pid fork_exec returns when no child was started (waitpid on it: ECHILD)."] [45 38 "// its own NUL message below"] [105 2 "// subprocess_fork_exec_impl's audit (queue 536): the executable list, the arguments and the environment as given"] [135 4 "// _Py_Gid_Converter, its failure \"invalid group id\"; -1 is no group here"] [175 2 "// the child's descriptors"] [203 3 "// a descriptor that is closed or close-on-exec needs no -1: the table ends at the last one that does, so"] [204 3 "// that ForkExec's descriptors above it stay under RLIMIT_NOFILE (test_no_leaking runs at the limit)"] [233 2 "// a pipe's end that is also a std number must not be closed by the -1 of its own number"] [267 2 "// restore_signals (py-os-1124; _Py_RestoreSignals in the child: SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ back to SIG_DFL, which the runtime"] [268 2 "// ignores since its start): ForkExec runs no code of ours in the child, but Go's child sets each signal Go handles"] [269 2 "// back to SIG_DFL (runtime_AfterForkInChild's clearSignalHandlers), so an ignored one is handled by Go (Notify) for the"] [270 2 "// fork and ignored again after; a child of restore_signals=False keeps them ignored (test_subprocess's"] [271 2 "// test_restore_signals)"] [309 1 "// restoreSignalsMu keeps one fork_exec at a time in restore_signals' window, where SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ are Go's."]] :go/pos {:name [3 9] :package [3 1]} :go/semis [[90 4] [95 46] [102 41] [106 74] [111 31] [165 35] [171 35] [191 44] [193 40] [206 13] [206 23] [213 49] [234 12] [234 19] [235 19] [272 32]]} (go/file "builtins_posixsubprocess.go" :build ["//go:build linux"] :imports [


